<!--
  010 V1 tray — light empty tray with grasping features.

  Authored in project 010; not a copy of the carried-over 007 object. The body is still
  named `payload` because that is the ROLE name the judges and the probe look up; which
  model fills the role is recorded per run (report.object).

  What is new versus the 007 tray:
    * a container instead of a solid box: floor + four walls + two dividers forming
      three separate pockets (PRECONDITIONS wants three part positions per tray);
    * a declared mass of 0.098 kg against the 007 tray's 0.210 kg.

  What is deliberately IDENTICAL: the grasp interface. The horizontal stems run to
  y = +-0.30 with 35 mm knobs, exactly as before, because the reach anchors and the
  hand-close preset were validated against that geometry. Changing the interface here
  would confound "a new tray" with "a new reach plan", and this round is meant to change
  only the object.

  Masses are declared per geom rather than derived from density, so the total is a
  statement the reader can check rather than a side effect of the meshes.
-->
<body name="payload" pos="0.23 0.0 0.85">
